@ [profile] cantor-sjs-commit-placement-acquisition/0.1

& [Requirements]
  + [CPA-001] strict request limits physical evidence receipt and fault forms deny unknown machine fields and enforce closed profiles
  + [CPA-002] request embeds one P2 journal of 1 through 32 links and pins repository root identifier branch HEAD object format exact Git executable raw executable SHA256 and positive limits
  + [CPA-003] unmodified P2 journal and receipt recomputation must pass before the first Git process
  + [CPA-004] request expected HEAD must equal the P2 open tip and final supplied carrier commit
  + [CPA-005] Git executable is an absolute canonical regular file whose raw SHA256 is checked before first and after final child process
  + [CPA-006] every child has a cleared environment fixed C locale no system/global config no prompt locks lazy fetch replacement objects attributes external diff text conversion or network protocol
  + [CPA-007] command vocabulary is closed to version repository identity raw commit tree listing and raw blob reads over exact supplied forty-hex identities and normalized paths
  + [CPA-008] pre and post repository root branch HEAD object format and Git directory identities are byte-equal and match the request
  + [CPA-009] stdout stderr command count request record blob and observation resources are hard bounded with concurrent pipe draining and first-fault refusal
  + [CPA-010] each raw carrier commit has exactly one tree header and exactly one parent equal to the P2 placement parent and record payload resulting commit
  + [CPA-011] each carrier tree has exactly one full-tree entry at the exact journal path with mode 100644 type blob and lowercase forty-hex object identity
  + [CPA-012] each raw blob equals compact serde JSON of the complete P2 record followed by exactly one LF and its byte count and SHA256 are independently recomputed
  + [CPA-013] ordered physical observations cover every P2 link exactly once and bind record placement carrier parent carrier commit tree path mode blob and canonical content identities
  + [CPA-014] receipt binds request P2 journal and P2 receipt executable repository pre/post observations command count observation_only physical_contact true nonauthority and self digest
  + [CPA-015] receipt validation independently replays all pure bindings and digest checks without Git contact
  + [CPA-016] CLI reads one bounded request file and emits one receipt to stdout only with typed first-fault JSON on stderr and no output path
  + [CPA-017] tests cover one-link multi-link deterministic replay plus T01 through T20 refusal families and unchanged repository/index state
  + [CPA-018] static and executable evidence prove no Git mutation output file hook network provider model MCP tool broker self-signature unsafe code dependency feature manifest or lockfile delta
  + [CPA-019] exact focused debug overflow-checked release workspace Clippy format recursive evidence local acceptance attribution commit and post-push gates pass
  + [CPA-020] live Cantor success is attempted only for an actual machine P2 record; otherwise typed unavailable with zero synthetic physical placement success

& [Constraints]
  + C01 safe Rust only and no new Cargo dependency
  + C02 reuse unmodified P2 forms validation and digest functions
  + C03 physical authority is observation_only and physical_contact true
  + C04 repository branch HEAD and object format are exact stable identities
  + C05 object profile is SHA-1 lowercase forty-hex matching P2
  + C06 carrier commits have exactly one parent and root or merge commits refuse
  + C07 tree entry mode is exactly 100644 and type exactly blob
  + C08 record encoding is serde_json compact UTF-8 plus exactly one LF
  + C09 raw bytes rather than worktree filters define equality
  + C10 journal path uses inherited normalized repository path rules
  + C11 command inputs contain no rev ranges ref expressions abbreviations or ambient names beyond fixed identity commands
  + C12 Git stderr is empty and any nonzero status refuses
  + C13 child environment and Git configuration are closed
  + C14 pre/post replay and executable hash equality are mandatory
  + C15 request and every process/output dimension are bounded
  + C16 receipt is deterministic and domain-separated
  + C17 CLI has no output path and writes no file
  + C18 fixture Git mutation occurs only in the external controlled test harness
  + C19 no provider contact or remote fallback
  + C20 no Cargo manifest lockfile feature or unsafe delta
  + C21 no foreign workspace custody
  + C22 no claim that P3 authorizes SWA-05 or proves operator intent signer trust remote state or future persistence

& [ImplementationBoundary]
  + one safe child module one stdout-only CLI unit integration/static tests controlled fixture runner evidence solution proof review narrative and publication bookend

& [SignatureState]
  + artifact lock proof review and satisfaction signature required before code
